1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,989
When light passes from one material into another, it bends. This is called refraction.

2
00:00:04,989 --> 00:00:09,577
A ray entering a glass block bends once on the way in, and again on the way out.

3
00:00:10,635 --> 00:00:15,510
Refraction happens because light travels at different speeds in different materials.

4
00:00:15,510 --> 00:00:21,302
It's fastest in air, slower in water and slowest in glass. We say glass has a higher optical density.

5
00:00:22,359 --> 00:00:27,234
When light slows down, it bends towards the normal. When it speeds up, it bends away.

6
00:00:28,291 --> 00:00:33,969
Think of a go-kart driving at an angle onto grass: the wheel that hits the grass first slows down,

7
00:00:33,969 --> 00:00:39,761
and the kart turns. If light hits the boundary straight on, along the normal, it doesn't bend at all.

8
00:00:40,819 --> 00:00:46,668
A coin lies at the bottom of an empty cup. You move your head back until the rim just hides the coin.

9
00:00:46,668 --> 00:00:51,486
Predict: what will you see if water is poured gently into the cup? Pause and decide.

10
00:00:52,543 --> 00:00:56,730
Watch. Your head stays still, and nothing changes while the cup is empty.

11
00:00:57,787 --> 00:01:02,719
As the water is poured in, the coin comes back into view, although you have not moved.

12
00:01:03,776 --> 00:01:07,906
Explain what you saw. Light from the coin travels up through the water.

13
00:01:07,906 --> 00:01:12,952
At the surface it passes from water into air, speeds up and bends away from the normal,

14
00:01:12,952 --> 00:01:14,788
over the rim and into your eye.

15
00:01:14,788 --> 00:01:20,236
Your brain traces the ray back in a straight line, so the coin seems higher than it really is.

16
00:01:20,236 --> 00:01:23,619
This is refraction. Pause and explain it in your own words.

17
00:01:24,677 --> 00:01:30,985
Refraction can fool us. Light from underwater speeds up as it leaves the water, bending away from the normal.

18
00:01:30,985 --> 00:01:36,778
So a pencil in water looks bent or broken, and a fish looks closer to the surface than it really is,

19
00:01:36,778 --> 00:01:38,441
which makes it hard to catch!

20
00:01:39,498 --> 00:01:41,047
Refraction is also useful.

21
00:01:41,047 --> 00:01:47,757
A camera lens is curved glass or plastic that bends light from each point of a scene so the rays meet on the sensor,

22
00:01:47,757 --> 00:01:49,018
forming a sharp image.

23
00:01:50,076 --> 00:01:55,065
And stars twinkle because their light is refracted again and again by the changing air.
